# .graphifyignore — patterns graphify skips when building the knowledge graph.
#
# Syntax is identical to .gitignore, including `!` negation. graphify reads the
# .gitignore in each directory automatically; when a .graphifyignore is present
# the two are merged and .graphifyignore patterns are evaluated LAST, so they
# win on conflict. A .graphifyignore can only ever exclude MORE — a `!` here
# cannot re-include a file that .gitignore already excluded. Scoping is
# per-directory, exactly like git: this file governs the repo root and below.

# --- graphify's own outputs (never graph the graph) ------------------------
# graph.json alone is ~3 MB; re-running `graphify update` would ingest its own
# output without this.
graphify-out/

# --- lockfile: generated dependency data, no product meaning ---------------
# package.json is the source of truth we actually want to see.
package-lock.json

# --- agent / tooling config — not product code -----------------------------
.claude/
.opencode/
.vscode/

# --- Expo / React starter-kit artwork with zero product references ---------
# Confirmed unused: 0 references in src/, app.json or app.config.ts.
assets/images/react-logo*.png
assets/images/tutorial-web.png
assets/images/tabIcons/

# Ignore the Expo template artwork as a group...
assets/images/expo-*
# ...but keep the Expo logo. The live animated splash still requires it from
# src/components/animated-icon.tsx and animated-icon.web.tsx, so the graph
# should keep that dependency edge.
!assets/images/expo-logo.png

# --- Deliberately KEPT — do not ignore -------------------------------------
# Punto brand assets are referenced by app.json / src and carry real meaning:
#   assets/images/icon.png              app.json  icon
#   assets/images/splash-icon.png       app.json  splash
#   assets/images/favicon.png           app.json  web favicon
#   assets/images/logo-glow.png         animated-icon splash glow
#   assets/images/android-icon-*.png    adaptive icon layers
#   assets/expo.icon/                   icon-composer source
